WEBVTT

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:13.310
I just think that I'll take it from here.

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:15.819
Goodbye.

00:04:15.819 --> 00:04:17.819
I think I'm finally ready for the front page.

00:04:17.819 --> 00:04:20.899
It's an article.

00:04:20.899 --> 00:04:22.899
I found a stack of missing persons cases

00:04:22.899 --> 00:04:24.899
that no one's talking about.

00:04:24.899 --> 00:04:26.899
There's similarities between them all.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.899
This city is being attacked and no one seems to care.

00:04:29.899 --> 00:04:33.899
Kind of makes you wish the red-blue blur wasn't sitting down on the job.

00:04:33.899 --> 00:04:38.180
I think that these people were attacked by the same criminal.

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:43.769
Now we can be the first to break this story.

00:04:43.769 --> 00:04:45.769
We can mourn the people of Metropolis.

00:04:45.769 --> 00:04:49.110
I can't print this.

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:50.110
You need to print it.

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:54.110
No, they're called facts, Clark, and you don't have any.

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:55.110
You don't care about these victims?

00:04:55.110 --> 00:05:03.449
Swooping this under the rug.

00:05:03.449 --> 00:05:06.449
Another conspiracy theory, because I love those.

00:05:06.449 --> 00:05:08.449
Look closely.

00:05:08.449 --> 00:05:11.449
You will not find a web of lies behind this facade.

00:05:11.449 --> 00:05:14.889
That would be your department.

00:05:14.889 --> 00:05:25.370
Man who's not afraid to cry.

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:28.370
Man who's not afraid to cut onions.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:31.370
You know, you still didn't have to cook me dinner.

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:33.370
Even though I did manage to override your settings,

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:35.370
retrieve all of your addresses,

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:36.370
and change your applications.

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:38.370
so the next time you go fishing for your phone

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:39.370
in your glove compartment,

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:41.370
you won't erase your whole world with the touch of one button.

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:44.370
Well, well, well, ain't you the most overachieving teacher's pet

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:46.370
know it all in the room?

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:48.370
He's got a sense of humor and he can cook.

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:49.370
Oh.

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:52.370
The one thing that was on the menu at the foster homes I grew up at?

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:54.370
Mac and cheese.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:06:00.720
So have you heard from Jimmy lately?

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:06.240
His last tirade of emails

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:09.240
included every single unflattering word in the dictionary,

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:13.240
including some that didn't get past the census.

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:17.240
I thought it'd be dying to get back together with you.

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:19.240
No.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:23.240
I believe that the last phrase he used was,

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:25.240
don't call me, don't come by,

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:27.240
and if you email me, I won't open it.

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:31.769
I thought we were best friends,

00:06:31.769 --> 00:06:34.769
but obviously there was some stuff

00:06:34.769 --> 00:06:36.769
brewing beneath the surface for a while.

00:06:36.769 --> 00:06:42.800
How can you be so close to someone

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:45.800
and not really know who they are?

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:51.889
Davis?

00:06:51.889 --> 00:06:55.490
No, it's fine.

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:56.490
It's fine.

00:06:56.490 --> 00:06:57.490
Really.

00:06:57.490 --> 00:07:11.740
Quick reflexes, huh?

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:14.790
Chloe.

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:15.790
Commatch?

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:20.310
Davis.

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:21.310
Clark?

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:25.420
Now that we have that all worked out.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:28.420
What's happening?

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:33.759
I was working on a story I thought you might have some information on.

00:07:33.759 --> 00:07:37.519
You know, I forgot something I was supposed to do.

00:07:37.519 --> 00:07:38.519
I should go.

00:07:38.519 --> 00:07:42.269
What about dinner?

00:07:42.269 --> 00:07:45.269
You know, I'll do it tomorrow.

00:07:45.269 --> 00:07:47.269
Call it leftovers.

00:07:47.269 --> 00:09:02.419
What's the prayer for dismembering a body?

00:09:02.419 --> 00:09:34.980
I can't believe this.

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:35.980
There were over a dozen missing persons.

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:36.980
There were over a dozen missing persons.

00:09:36.980 --> 00:09:37.980
last month alone.

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:39.980
I think it'd be newsworthy.

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:43.980
Yeah, since when did Newsworthy have anything to do with what was on the front page?

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:53.509
You know, Clark, I really hope you have the safety cocked on your heat vision.

00:09:53.509 --> 00:09:55.509
What?

00:09:55.509 --> 00:10:01.950
You've been staring at the back of my head so hard, I'm afraid my hair's going to go up in flames.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:04.950
I just didn't know you and Davis were spending so much time together.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:08.899
If you don't want to talk about it.

00:10:08.899 --> 00:10:09.899
No, please.

00:10:09.899 --> 00:10:11.899
I love trudging through stagnant water.

00:10:11.899 --> 00:10:15.899
It just seems like you're moving on kind of fast, and I don't get what you see in the guy.

00:10:15.899 --> 00:10:16.899
First of all,

00:10:16.899 --> 00:10:21.899
it was dinner. And secondly, he's kind, supportive, and a strong shoulder for me to lean on,

00:10:21.899 --> 00:10:24.899
which I don't know if you've actually realized, but I could really use right now.

00:10:24.899 --> 00:10:28.899
Look, it's just I have a bad feeling about the guy. I mean, come on, Chloe.

00:10:28.899 --> 00:10:34.899
Don't Chloe me, me, Clark. What is it with this whole meet me out in the back for a dual mentality?

00:10:34.899 --> 00:10:38.899
It might have something to do with the fact that this guy disappears and can't explain where he went.

00:10:38.899 --> 00:10:41.899
He's full of secrets, Chloe. There's not even a record of his childhood.

00:10:41.899 --> 00:10:43.899
Sounds familiar.

00:10:43.899 --> 00:10:46.899
I don't collect morbid crime scene photos in my locker.

00:10:46.899 --> 00:10:52.850
I'm not the first EMT to show up at every gruesome murder.

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:53.850
What is it?

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:56.850
A vehicle was found on fire just outside of Smallville.

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:59.850
It has Davis's license plates.

00:10:59.850 --> 00:11:15.840
Were you expecting a chorus of angels?

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:17.840
I'm sorry to disappoint you.

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:22.950
I wanted to be here when you woke up.

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:26.950
I apologize for the state that you're in.

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:33.179
I didn't expect you to end up like this.

00:11:33.179 --> 00:11:39.980
I was trying to kill you.

00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:41.980
That seems to be harder than I thought.

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:54.440
You're safe with me, safer than out there.

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:56.440
If the world knew you were a serial killer,

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:59.440
you'd be running from torches for the rest of your life.

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:03.440
You got the wrong idea about me, lady.

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:08.440
It's not your fault that you were born with a killer instinct.

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:14.299
I even admire your altruistic selection of victims.

00:12:14.299 --> 00:12:20.299
It's like keeping bats around to wipe out the parasites that prey on the city.

00:12:20.299 --> 00:12:28.529
I know you've tried.

00:12:28.529 --> 00:12:32.639
to absolve yourself.

00:12:32.639 --> 00:12:36.639
Even suicide wouldn't really work for a guy who can't die, would it?

00:12:36.639 --> 00:12:46.549
I am not.

00:12:46.549 --> 00:12:48.549
You're not who you think you are.

00:12:48.549 --> 00:12:58.149
And today, you proved my theory.

00:12:58.149 --> 00:13:02.149
After I discovered that you'd been a little unfriendly

00:13:02.149 --> 00:13:05.149
to a few metropolis citizens,

00:13:05.149 --> 00:13:08.149
I started looking into your background.

00:13:08.149 --> 00:13:12.149
The only problem is you don't have one.

00:13:12.149 --> 00:13:13.149
I think.

00:13:13.149 --> 00:13:18.679
I thought I'd hit a dead end until I inherited this.

00:13:18.679 --> 00:13:20.679
Stolen, if I'm being honest.

00:13:20.679 --> 00:13:25.629
I thought this might jog your rusty memory.

00:13:25.629 --> 00:13:29.230
It was Lionel Luther's.

00:13:29.230 --> 00:13:34.580
It tells a fascinating story about a boy who fell to earth

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:37.580
the day a media shower destroyed a small Kansas town.

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:44.460
I'm beginning to believe the boy did not come here alone.

00:13:44.460 --> 00:14:11.129
Not in the sky, Martha.

00:14:11.129 --> 00:14:13.129
And where did he come?

00:14:13.129 --> 00:14:17.129
I don't know, but he must have parents.

00:14:17.129 --> 00:14:20.789
He must have parents.

00:14:20.789 --> 00:14:22.789
Well, if he does, they're definitely not from Kansas.

00:14:22.789 --> 00:14:27.450
Sweetheart, we can't keep him.

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:29.450
We're gonna tell people.

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:31.450
We found him out in the field.

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:33.450
We didn't find him.

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:35.759
He found us.

00:14:35.759 --> 00:15:41.299
There's...

00:15:41.299 --> 00:17:29.099
What are you doing in here?

00:17:29.099 --> 00:17:31.099
A man brought me here a few days ago.

00:17:31.099 --> 00:17:38.160
He made them put needles in me.

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:40.160
But you don't look sick.

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:49.940
Do you want to play?

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:51.940
My dad went to some farm.

00:17:51.940 --> 00:18:07.759
The day the meteor shower struck Smallville,

00:18:07.759 --> 00:18:08.759
Linal sent out of a day.

00:18:08.759 --> 00:18:13.609
a search party for you.

00:18:13.609 --> 00:18:15.609
Lionel had you taken from that field

00:18:15.609 --> 00:18:18.609
because he thought you were a prophesied Messiah

00:18:18.609 --> 00:18:20.609
called the traveler.

00:18:20.609 --> 00:18:24.609
A visitor from another planet sent to save humankind.

00:18:24.609 --> 00:18:27.609
But what Lionel didn't realize

00:18:27.609 --> 00:18:33.299
is that there were two boys that fell to Earth that day.

00:18:33.299 --> 00:18:34.299
The traveler.

00:18:34.299 --> 00:18:58.079
Excuse me.

00:18:58.079 --> 00:19:01.680
Have the police been here yet?

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:02.680
Come and gone.

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:06.279
Did they find a victim?

00:19:06.279 --> 00:19:08.279
The thing was abandoned.

00:19:08.279 --> 00:19:09.279
No sign of a driver.

00:19:09.279 --> 00:19:12.839
Thank you.

00:19:12.839 --> 00:19:24.569
What's going on?

00:19:24.569 --> 00:19:27.569
It's weird that Davis would have stopped here.

00:19:27.569 --> 00:19:28.569
Why?

00:19:28.569 --> 00:19:30.569
What's here?

00:19:30.569 --> 00:19:32.569
This is a field with my ship landed.

00:19:32.569 --> 00:19:38.579
That's a pretty big coincidence pill to swallow.

00:19:38.579 --> 00:19:45.700
This place must hold a lot of memories for you, huh?

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:56.990
Chloe, memories aren't the only thing buried in that field.

00:19:56.990 --> 00:21:11.980
Remember of St. George.

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:14.980
He slayed dragons with his sword called.

00:21:14.980 --> 00:21:21.950
I'm St. George, and you are the dragon.

00:21:21.950 --> 00:21:23.950
You have been sent to destroy the world,

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:24.950
but only I can...

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:28.950
protected from a beast like you.

00:21:28.950 --> 00:21:31.950
Fight or die.

00:21:44.049 --> 00:21:50.220
Slade, I'm the victor, and I shall claim my treasure.

00:21:50.220 --> 00:22:27.200
You think you can keep me here?

00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:30.200
I know. There's nothing that can restrain you.

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:36.869
But what are you going to do?

00:22:36.869 --> 00:22:39.869
I've been asking myself that question for the last few hours.

00:22:39.869 --> 00:22:44.859
What do you do when you find Judas in your midst?

00:22:44.859 --> 00:22:50.390
Who would Christ have been if Judas had not betrayed him?

00:22:50.390 --> 00:22:51.390
Maybe we would remember Jesus as...

00:22:51.390 --> 00:22:54.390
remember Jesus as only a teacher roaming the desert.

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:57.670
I don't quite understand what you're getting at.

00:22:57.670 --> 00:23:00.670
Without Judas, Jesus would have never risen from the dead

00:23:00.670 --> 00:23:08.160
to come back and face his greatest challenge, saving humankind.

00:23:08.160 --> 00:23:12.789
There is a savior among us.

00:23:12.789 --> 00:23:15.789
You are here to betray him.

00:23:15.789 --> 00:23:20.380
I haven't betrayed anyone.

00:23:20.380 --> 00:23:25.579
I finally realized that until you fulfill your destiny,

00:23:25.579 --> 00:23:28.579
he won't have his great challenge to overcome.

00:23:28.579 --> 00:23:32.579
He cannot become the world's savior without triumping over the world's

00:23:32.579 --> 00:23:40.059
triumphing over the world's destroyer.

00:23:40.059 --> 00:23:42.059
What are you talking about?

00:23:42.059 --> 00:23:44.059
Clark.

00:23:44.059 --> 00:23:47.059
There's a reason that you two don't get along.

00:23:47.059 --> 00:24:04.740
You were destined to kill each other.

00:24:04.740 --> 00:24:07.740
The guy blacks out regularly, and you chose not to mention it.

00:24:07.740 --> 00:24:09.740
I figured he had low blood sugar or something.

00:24:09.740 --> 00:24:12.740
He told you he was hiding something dark inside, Chloe.

00:24:12.740 --> 00:24:13.740
That didn't set off any alarms for you.

00:24:13.740 --> 00:24:16.740
You know what? I figured dark meant moody or bipolar at worst.

00:24:16.740 --> 00:24:19.740
I don't exactly jump right to serial killer.

00:24:19.740 --> 00:24:21.740
And all the times that you were angry at me for doubting him.

00:24:21.740 --> 00:24:22.740
I know.

00:24:22.740 --> 00:24:24.740
I was in denial.

00:24:24.740 --> 00:24:29.740
You know, I couldn't believe that it was this bad.

00:24:29.740 --> 00:24:31.740
It's not that bad, Chloe.

00:24:31.740 --> 00:24:35.339
It's worse.

00:24:35.339 --> 00:24:37.339
I just can't believe he's the serial killer that...

00:24:37.339 --> 00:24:40.680
That Jimmy won us a bell.

00:24:40.680 --> 00:24:47.220
I did some checking into these missing persons.

00:24:47.220 --> 00:24:50.220
They're not exactly Metropolis's finest.

00:24:50.220 --> 00:24:52.220
Assault charges, breaking and entering abuse.

00:24:52.220 --> 00:24:55.220
Do you think Davis is on some sort of vigilante mission?

00:24:55.220 --> 00:24:56.220
He wasn't until last night.

00:24:56.220 --> 00:25:00.220
I mean, he's not stupid enough to abandon his car next to a...

00:25:00.220 --> 00:25:01.220
A field floor.

00:25:01.220 --> 00:25:02.220
of evidence.

00:25:02.220 --> 00:25:05.220
Chloe, I get the feeling someone took him.

00:25:05.220 --> 00:25:07.220
When I was looking into Davis's past,

00:25:07.220 --> 00:25:10.220
his county records had already been checked out by someone.

00:25:10.220 --> 00:25:20.079
I think it's time to pay a visit to the widow of Luther Corp.

00:25:20.079 --> 00:25:21.079
We tried to stop him.

00:25:21.079 --> 00:25:22.079
We opened fire, but he...

00:25:22.079 --> 00:25:23.079
Find him.

00:25:23.079 --> 00:25:34.039
Or don't come back.

00:25:34.039 --> 00:25:37.039
Tess, I know you've been looking into Davis pool.

00:25:37.039 --> 00:25:39.039
He did this, didn't he?

00:25:39.039 --> 00:25:42.039
I'm afraid there's not a short version of that story.

00:25:42.039 --> 00:25:45.480
I think I missed something.

00:25:45.480 --> 00:25:46.480
No, you've been at the center of it the whole time.

00:25:46.480 --> 00:25:49.480
center of it the whole time.

00:25:49.480 --> 00:25:52.480
I came into possession of a journal of Lionel Luther's.

00:25:52.480 --> 00:25:57.480
The journal talks about a boy who fell from the stars on the day of a meteor shower.

00:25:57.480 --> 00:26:02.480
Lionel's obsession with this traveler was the only reason that he was in Smallville that day.

00:26:02.480 --> 00:26:06.480
He wanted to possess the traveler for himself.

00:26:06.480 --> 00:26:08.480
Why are you telling me all this?

00:26:08.480 --> 00:26:14.500
Because Lionel and then Lex got the moral of the story wrong.

00:26:14.500 --> 00:26:18.480
According to the Kowachi Indians, this boy is part of a two-headed

00:26:18.500 --> 00:26:21.500
good and evil.

00:26:21.500 --> 00:26:25.500
The Luthers were too busy feuding over which one of them was worthy enough

00:26:25.500 --> 00:26:29.500
to be your adversary that they couldn't see the truth,

00:26:29.500 --> 00:26:35.150
that there was another boy who came to Earth with you.

00:26:35.150 --> 00:26:39.490
Davis Bloom.

00:26:39.490 --> 00:26:46.339
So you think that Davis Bloom and I are from another planet?

00:26:46.339 --> 00:26:49.339
Lionel found Davis on the day of the meteor shower.

00:26:49.339 --> 00:26:53.339
He thought he was the traveler, but then the boy's test seemed normal.

00:26:53.339 --> 00:26:55.339
Lionel was holding Davis.

00:26:55.339 --> 00:26:56.339
Only for him.

00:26:56.339 --> 00:26:57.339
for five days.

00:26:57.339 --> 00:26:59.339
And then he threw the boy out onto the street

00:26:59.339 --> 00:27:02.339
because he got a phone call from Martha Kent.

00:27:02.339 --> 00:27:06.059
As you're reaching.

00:27:06.059 --> 00:27:07.059
Am I?

00:27:07.059 --> 00:27:09.059
It's Lionel's own words.

00:27:09.059 --> 00:27:12.059
And I quote, I have the wrong boy.

00:27:12.059 --> 00:27:16.059
But I believe that I have found the true traveler.

00:27:16.059 --> 00:27:19.059
Why else would Lionel Luther arrange an adoption

00:27:19.059 --> 00:27:21.059
for a boy who seemed to come out of nowhere?

00:27:21.059 --> 00:27:40.230
Looks like you're the reason that Davis was abandoned in the first place.

00:27:40.230 --> 00:27:42.230
What do the Luther Corp, Deva have to say?

00:27:42.230 --> 00:27:46.910
I know what you have to say?

00:27:46.910 --> 00:27:48.910
done. Jimmy was right.

00:27:48.910 --> 00:27:52.910
Uh, that guy that I killed.

00:27:52.910 --> 00:27:55.910
He was a drunk driver. He was a three-time offender.

00:27:55.910 --> 00:27:56.910
And what about all the others?

00:27:56.910 --> 00:27:59.910
Are you going to try and justify killing them too?

00:27:59.910 --> 00:28:01.910
No, I didn't know what else to do!

00:28:01.910 --> 00:28:04.910
You lied to me!

00:28:04.910 --> 00:28:07.910
I had to! I didn't want to drag you into all of the street!

00:28:07.910 --> 00:28:08.910
Then why are you here?

00:28:08.910 --> 00:28:20.140
I love you. And I need to know if you care about me.

00:28:20.140 --> 00:28:27.420
You ask me that. I thought I did.

00:28:27.420 --> 00:28:37.000
I won't do anything.

00:28:37.000 --> 00:28:38.000
I won't do anything.

00:28:38.000 --> 00:28:39.000
for you.

00:28:39.000 --> 00:29:14.589
Dr. Grohl's lab.

00:29:14.589 --> 00:29:16.589
Chloe.

00:29:16.589 --> 00:30:20.890
Life, Clark.

00:30:20.890 --> 00:30:22.890
You can take it if I choose.

00:30:22.890 --> 00:30:24.890
Davis, don't be a martyr.

00:30:24.890 --> 00:30:26.890
That's not what this is, Clark.

00:30:26.890 --> 00:30:28.890
I'm not doing this for you.

00:30:28.890 --> 00:30:29.890
I want this to end.

00:30:29.890 --> 00:30:32.890
I can't live with myself.

00:30:32.890 --> 00:30:34.890
It's not your fault.

00:30:34.890 --> 00:30:37.890
Everything that's happened to you is because of me.

00:30:37.890 --> 00:30:40.890
All right? We should have been brothers.

00:30:40.890 --> 00:30:43.890
Davis, you didn't have a home.

00:30:43.890 --> 00:30:44.890
That would have happened to me.

00:30:44.890 --> 00:30:47.890
I've always wondered what it would have been like.

00:30:47.890 --> 00:30:49.890
If did Luthers had found me in that field.

00:30:49.890 --> 00:30:52.890
I could have turned out differently.

00:30:52.890 --> 00:30:54.890
But you didn't.

00:30:54.890 --> 00:30:57.890
You were destined to have the better life.

00:30:57.890 --> 00:31:00.890
No matter how hard we try to fight it,

00:31:00.890 --> 00:31:04.890
we will always return to our true nature.

00:31:04.890 --> 00:31:11.990
Chloe, pull the lever. Let me end this.

00:31:11.990 --> 00:31:13.990
No, Chloe, you have to give this another chance.

00:31:13.990 --> 00:31:15.990
This is not set in stone.

00:31:15.990 --> 00:31:16.990
Enough, clerk.

00:31:16.990 --> 00:31:17.990
Clark.

00:31:17.990 --> 00:31:21.990
You know that you should let me die.

00:31:21.990 --> 00:31:24.990
Davis, there has to be something in your life.

00:31:24.990 --> 00:31:27.990
Something that is worth giving it one more try.

00:31:27.990 --> 00:31:37.869
It isn't always about.

00:31:37.869 --> 00:31:41.910
It's about...

00:31:41.910 --> 00:32:10.150
You'll get me right downshy!

00:32:10.150 --> 00:32:52.339
What are we doing here?

00:32:52.339 --> 00:32:55.339
I was told to drop you off here.

00:32:55.339 --> 00:32:58.970
To meet me.

00:32:58.970 --> 00:34:18.730
How are you holding up?

00:34:18.730 --> 00:34:20.730
I've had better days.

00:34:20.730 --> 00:34:29.190
I'm not saying a lot in Smallville.

00:34:29.190 --> 00:34:34.940
And Davis is...

00:34:34.940 --> 00:34:43.380
I spoke to Oliver. He's taking care of the details.

00:34:43.380 --> 00:34:48.639
We need to talk about what happened.

00:34:48.639 --> 00:34:51.949
I wouldn't change what I did.

00:34:51.949 --> 00:34:54.949
But there's always another way.

00:34:54.949 --> 00:34:56.949
He could have killed you, Clark.

00:34:56.949 --> 00:35:02.679
I won't risk the safety of the world because of your code of ethics.

00:35:02.679 --> 00:35:06.679
Because you refuse to stop the things that threaten you.

00:35:06.679 --> 00:35:17.329
Jovel said he was the ultimate destroyer.

00:35:17.329 --> 00:35:19.329
Didn't turn out to be much of a fight.

00:35:19.329 --> 00:35:41.519
When I was a kid, I used to have this nightmare.

00:35:41.519 --> 00:35:46.829
nightmare. My ship landed in a field and no one ever found me.

00:35:46.829 --> 00:35:49.829
That nightmare was Davis's life.

00:35:49.829 --> 00:35:55.010
I always felt like it was a burden knowing that I was destined to save people.

00:35:55.010 --> 00:36:01.760
I can't imagine what it must have felt like, knowing that no matter how you lived your life,

00:36:01.760 --> 00:36:23.820
you were doomed.

00:36:23.820 --> 00:36:25.820
The new contemplative Clark Kent.

00:36:25.820 --> 00:36:27.820
I like it.

00:36:27.820 --> 00:36:29.820
Kind of busy.

00:36:29.820 --> 00:36:31.820
With what? Farm chores?

00:36:31.820 --> 00:36:38.360
I'd let you off if you were saving a busload of children, but...

00:36:38.360 --> 00:36:39.340
cleaning the feet.

00:36:39.360 --> 00:36:40.360
been?

00:36:40.360 --> 00:36:44.360
I'm really sorry that you bought into this strange obsession

00:36:44.360 --> 00:36:46.360
that the Luther's had for me, but...

00:36:46.360 --> 00:36:47.360
I don't think of it as buying in.

00:36:47.360 --> 00:36:51.280
I think of it as believing.

00:36:51.280 --> 00:36:54.280
You choose to spend your Saturday nights reading the journal of a madman.

00:36:54.280 --> 00:36:57.280
Sounds to me like you have a few holes in your personal life.

00:36:57.280 --> 00:37:00.980
We all look to idols.

00:37:00.980 --> 00:37:05.980
Religion, the rich and the famous because we have holes in our lives.

00:37:05.980 --> 00:37:08.980
It doesn't mean that these things aren't real.

00:37:08.980 --> 00:37:13.539
What you've made me out to be is not real.

00:37:14.539 --> 00:37:16.539
I'll never be that man.

00:37:16.539 --> 00:37:18.539
Not until Judas is at your bed.

00:37:18.539 --> 00:37:25.489
I have this feeling that you'll never fulfill your great destiny

00:37:25.489 --> 00:37:29.119
until you meet your greatest challenge.

00:37:29.119 --> 00:37:31.119
You don't know anything about my life.

00:37:31.119 --> 00:37:34.980
If this is the way that you lied to Lex,

00:37:34.980 --> 00:37:37.980
then I can see how it pushed him over the edge.

00:37:37.980 --> 00:37:41.980
Lex was racing toward that drop off way before he met me.

00:37:41.980 --> 00:37:43.980
I have a betrayal.

00:37:43.980 --> 00:37:49.059
You know the more you love someone, the harder it is.

00:37:49.059 --> 00:37:51.059
Are you threatening me?

00:37:51.059 --> 00:37:54.170
I'm not that naive.

00:37:54.170 --> 00:37:58.139
That naive.

00:37:58.139 --> 00:38:00.139
I'm not some problem to be solved.

00:38:00.139 --> 00:38:02.550
I get it.

00:38:02.550 --> 00:38:05.500
It's too early.

00:38:05.500 --> 00:38:12.309
Just know that I'll wait for you, Clark.

00:38:12.309 --> 00:38:14.309
I'll wait for you to come to me.

00:38:14.309 --> 00:38:28.469
It's gonna be a long way.

00:38:28.469 --> 00:38:30.469
It'll be shorter than you think, Cal L.

00:38:30.469 --> 00:40:10.769
Don't be afraid.

00:40:10.769 --> 00:40:41.639
No matter what you want is Davis,

00:40:41.639 --> 00:40:43.639
the other side of you will still try and kill him.

00:40:43.639 --> 00:40:45.639
I won't kill Clark if I'm with you.

00:40:45.639 --> 00:40:52.500
I have to do with any of this.

00:40:52.500 --> 00:40:55.539
Around you.

00:40:55.539 --> 00:40:58.539
That seems to calm the murder inside me.

00:40:58.539 --> 00:41:03.070
But you said so yourself, it's your true nature.

00:41:03.070 --> 00:41:08.070
Strong.

00:41:08.070 --> 00:41:10.070
out there than my need to kill.

